# Hard cases: the failures that real sessions and reviews turned up, written again in
# our own words so nothing in this file comes from anyone's conversation. Each scene is
# one kind of bug. `pnpm check` plays this file like a demo, judges every scene at rest,
# and for each line of words hides it and looks at what the screen loses (its footprint).
# It is not offered in the app: it is the check's own script.

look paper

# a long line is kept whole: the last word must be on the stage
scene long layout=stack lines=2 brisk
say long | A good answer is sometimes long, and the stage has to carry every word of it without cutting the end off at some invisible limit, because a reader who is halfway through a sentence cannot tell that the rest was thrown away. So this line goes on well past three hundred and twenty characters, through clauses and commas and a few small asides, to prove that nothing is clipped, and it ends on the word zebra.
say | Short lines still sit under it.
wait 1

# Japanese and Korean: the glyphs are drawn, not a question mark each
scene scripts layout=stack lines=4
say ja | 日本語の文章も、正しい字で表示されます。
say ko | 한국어 문장도 올바른 글자로 표시됩니다.
say title size=xxl | 漢字と한글
say zh | 学习汉字需要耐心和时间
wait 1

# a flowchart with multi-word edge labels and cross-links
scene flow layout=caption
flow car right | How a car's core parts connect
node tank | Fuel tank
node pump from=tank | Fuel pump
node engine from=pump:fuel | Engine
node rad | Radiator
node exh from=engine:burnt gas | Exhaust
node gear from=engine:turning | Gearbox and clutch
node shaft from=gear | Driveshaft and differential
node wheels end from=shaft | Wheels
node battery | Battery
node starter from=battery | Starter motor
node alt from=engine:belt drive | Alternator
node ecu note | ECU computer
node pedal | Brake pedal
node brakes from=pedal:brake fluid | Calipers and discs
link rad engine both | coolant loop
link starter engine | cranks it
link alt battery | charges it
link ecu engine dashed | times fuel and spark
link brakes wheels | slow them
wait 1

# words beside strokes: labels and a narration line that no drawn line may run through
scene beside layout=figure
line road 6,60 94,60 thick=2
line river 8,12 92,40 thick=2
line fence 50,6 50,66 thick=1
circle well 22,36 5 fill=accent
say label near=road:below | the old road
say label near=river:above | the river bend
say label near=fence:right | the fence line
say label near=well leader=yes | the well
say aside | The narration must stand clear of every line drawn here.
wait 1

# a column of digits lined up on their right edge
scene digits layout=free canvas=square
say h at=70,12 align=right size=s ink=dim | Total
say d1 at=70,26 align=right | 1,204
say d2 at=70,40 align=right | 98
say d3 at=70,54 align=right | 7,310.5
say d4 at=70,68 align=right | 12
say d5 at=70,84 align=right size=l | 8,624.5
wait 1

# many labels crowded round one part
scene crowd layout=figure
rect body 50,24 60x40 fill=dim
circle eye 64,36 4 fill=accent
circle mouth 80,54 4 fill=accent
circle ear 106,36 4 fill=accent
say label near=eye leader=yes | eye
say label near=mouth leader=yes | mouth
say label near=ear leader=yes | ear
say aside | Three labels, three leaders, none across another.
wait 1

# more lines than a small stage likes: every one of them stays
scene many layout=stack lines=8 brisk
say | First line of eight.
say | Second line of eight.
say | Third line of eight.
say | Fourth line of eight.
say | Fifth line of eight.
say | Sixth line of eight.
say | Seventh line of eight.
say | Eighth line of eight.
wait 1

# fb-051: a slider bound to moves to points (and a shape drawn again) moves every shape it names as it is dragged, half way at half way (the check drags it with real pointer events), and a control whose binds change nothing is told
scene fb-051 layout=figure lines=3
circle fbdisc 60,40 18 stroke=ink thick=0.4
circle fbdot 50,32 3 fill=accent
circle fbring 44,44 2 fill=ink
rect fbbar 62,46 12x4 fill=ink
path fbleaf fill=accent | M 52 52 L 60 48 L 58 58 Z
group fbpair
circle fbp1 82,30 2 fill=accent in=fbpair
circle fbp2 88,30 2 fill=ink in=fbpair
card fbtools | Try it
slider fbspin 0 90 0 unit=deg in=fbtools | Turn it
toggle fbmark on in=fbtools | Marker
bind fbspin | move fbdot 72,32
bind fbspin | move fbbar 46,54
bind fbspin | move fbleaf 76,60
bind fbspin | move fbpair 100,56
bind fbspin | circle fbring 78,44 2 fill=ink
bind fbmark=on | set fbdot opacity=1
wait 1

# fb-054: a choice that has left the stage and is written again by its id (a revise that came after it had played is this `correct`) is a choice with the new words, not plain words nobody can tap
scene fb-054 layout=caption brisk
say fbc1 choice | Spec the sphere
say fbc2 choice | Write the test
drop fbc1
drop fbc2
wait 1
correct fbc1 | Spec the bindable transforms first
correct fbc2 | Which matters most to you?

# a dark look with small dim notes: they must still read
scene dark layout=figure
look night
rect panel 30,20 100x50 fill=dim
say label near=panel:above | A dim note on a dark ground
say label near=panel:below size=s ink=dim | a smaller dimmer one
wait 1

# fb-058: the column sum is a `math` line the painter works out, not digits placed by hand (so the carries line up): a worked example, then her own sum with its boxes blank, then asks that wait their turn
scene fb-058 layout=stack brisk
math w1 column worked | 4768 + 2557
math m1 column | 3486 + 2795
ask q1 is=7043 stage=1 | 5079 + 1964 = __
ask q2 is=10000 stage=2:q1 | 6358 + 3642 = __
wait 0.5

# fb-060: asks that wait for the one before them draw nothing: no number, no blank, no room taken from the words round them
scene fb-060 layout=free canvas=square brisk
say t1 title enter=cut | Adding big numbers
say s1 at=50,30 enter=cut | Line up the columns and add. @with
say s2 at=50,44 enter=cut | Start with the ones. @with
ask q1 is=6281 stage=1 | 3486 + 2795 = __
ask q2 is=7043 stage=2:q1 | 5079 + 1964 = __
ask q3 is=10000 stage=3:q2 | 6358 + 3642 = __
wait 0.5

# fb-061: an ask written with a step among its answers (and a thousands comma) still works: it accepts the one answer, the hint that names a step stays, and the line says why
scene fb-061 layout=stack brisk
say s1 enter=cut | Add 3,486 and 2,795, the ones first.
ask q1 is=6,281,6 stage=1 | 3486 + 2795 = __
hint in=q1 stage=yes | Start right: 6 + 5. Is that more than 9? What do you write, and what do you carry?
wait 0.5

# fb-059: a title with no at= in a free scene goes to the top of the stage, never over what is drawn
scene fb-059 layout=free canvas=square brisk
say t1 title enter=cut | Adding big numbers
say d1 at=60,28 align=right face=mono enter=cut | 4768 @with
say d2 at=60,42 align=right face=mono enter=cut | 2557 @with
path rl stroke=ink enter=cut | M34,50 L62,50 @with
say d3 at=60,58 align=right face=mono ink=accent enter=cut | 7325 @with
say n1 aside at=84,28 enter=cut | 1. Line up the columns. @with
say n2 aside at=84,44 enter=cut | 2. Add from the right. @with
wait 0.5

# fb-025: an app whose code reaches for d3 and never says `uses=`. The host loads the library all the same (and d3-geo is on the shelf), so the globe is drawn.
# The scene asks for nothing on its app line: if the frame ever stops hearing that, d3 is not defined, the script throws, and the frame shows an empty ground.
scene fb-025 layout=caption
app globe height=300 | A globe, drawn with D3
row globe | <style>
row globe | body { margin: 0; overflow: hidden; }
row globe | svg { display: block; width: 100vw; height: 100vh; }
row globe | .sea { fill: var(--accent); }
row globe | .grat { fill: none; stroke: var(--ground); stroke-opacity: 0.5; }
row globe | .land { fill: var(--ink); }
row globe | </style>
row globe | <svg id="s"></svg>
row globe | <script>
row globe | var w = innerWidth, h = innerHeight, svg = d3.select('#s');
row globe | var proj = d3.geoOrthographic().scale(Math.min(w, h) * 0.45).translate([w / 2, h / 2]).rotate([-10, -20]);
row globe | var path = d3.geoPath(proj);
row globe | svg.append('path').attr('class', 'sea').datum({ type: 'Sphere' }).attr('d', path);
row globe | svg.append('path').attr('class', 'grat').datum(d3.geoGraticule10()).attr('d', path);
row globe | svg.append('path').attr('class', 'land').datum(d3.geoCircle().center([10, 15]).radius(28)()).attr('d', path);
row globe | </script>
say c1 | A globe, from D3.
wait 1

# fb-025, the other half: an app that throws. This one paints, then throws on purpose. The frame tells the page, the page tells the server, and the brain's next brief says
# `app fixthrow threw: "…" (line 8)`. The check reads that back from the session's own log.
scene fb-025-throws layout=caption
app fixthrow height=200 | A fixture that throws on purpose
row fixthrow | <style>
row fixthrow | body { margin: 0; background: #1f3a5f; color: #ffffff; font: 16px sans-serif; }
row fixthrow | p { margin: 0; padding: 24px; }
row fixthrow | </style>
row fixthrow | <p>This app paints, and then throws.</p>
row fixthrow | <script>
row fixthrow | var seen = 0;
row fixthrow | throw new Error('fixture: thrown on purpose');
row fixthrow | </script>
say c1 | An app that throws.
wait 1

# fb-025, the third way to show nothing: no error, and nothing drawn but a flat ground. Three seconds after it loads the page looks at it and tells the brain it drew nothing.
scene fb-025-blank layout=caption
app fixblank height=200 | A fixture that draws nothing
row fixblank | <style>
row fixblank | body { margin: 0; background: #1f3a5f; }
row fixblank | canvas { display: block; width: 100vw; height: 100vh; }
row fixblank | </style>
row fixblank | <canvas id="c"></canvas>
row fixblank | <script>
row fixblank | var c = document.getElementById('c'), x = c.getContext('2d');
row fixblank | c.width = innerWidth; c.height = innerHeight;
row fixblank | x.fillStyle = '#1f3a5f'; x.fillRect(0, 0, c.width, c.height);
row fixblank | </script>
say c1 | An app that draws nothing.
wait 1

# a photo with callouts at spots. The check puts a generated test pattern up as u1 (900 by 600) and, as the server does for a photo a turn carries, the shape is stamped: aspect=1.5

scene photo layout=figure canvas=wide
pic p1 from=u1 aspect=1.5
say c1 callout at=8,10 in=p1 | top left
say c2 callout at=92,12 in=p1 | top right
say c3 callout at=50,50 in=p1 | middle
say c4 callout at=20,78 in=p1 | low left
say c5 callout at=81,90 in=p1 | bottom right
say c6 callout at=50,8 in=p1 | top middle
say c7 callout at=3,50 in=p1 | left edge
say c8 callout at=97,55 in=p1 | right edge
wait 1
